A||||35||Kelvin Vivian||FYI: Unique features of each year...||||1||
Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||04-18-2001||02:05 PM||||These are what I can think of right now...<P>1984: <BR>Only year "Indy Fiero" model is offered.<BR>Voltmeter in tach.<BR>Manual 4-cyls have a 4-spd tranny.<BR>Magnesium engine vent in center of rear decklid.<BR>Quarter windows are made of glass.<BR>4-cyl Dukes do not have roller-lifters.<P>1985:<BR>The only year the "GT" model doesn't have the fastback.<BR>Only year all manual V6 Fieros have the 4-spd tranny.<P>1986:<BR>???<P>1987:<BR>Blue exterior is only offered this year.<P>1988:<BR>Only year "Formula" model is offered.<BR>"SE" model is no longer avaliable.<BR>Yellow exterior is only offered this year.<BR>4-cyl Dukes have counter-rotating balance shafts.<BR>Monotone paint scheme on all Fiero models.<BR>Revised front and rear suspension & rear cradle design.||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||04-18-2001||02:14 PM||||1984-uniquely the only year to start on fire consistently.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-18-2001||02:19 PM||||85 and 86 V-6 have 4-spd. 5 spd put in near the end of the 86 production run. <BR>Gold is only 86 and 87 for exterior color.<BR>86 first year of GT fastback<BR>87 first year of larger gas tank<BR>88 suspension re-design, different wheel offsets for 15" wheels, and vented brakes.<BR>87 "duke" was now a DIS ignition system.<BR>86 First year for stock subwoofer (Premium sound)<BR>86 first year for gauges above radio pod.<BR>86 first year for 3rd brake light<BR>86 first year for sail panel speakers<BR>85 Silver color added<BR>87 First year of re-designed front and rear bumpers. <BR>84 only year for fleece/suede seats.<BR>88 Only year that does not have the trunk aux fan with a V-6.<P>That's all I can think of right away.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bluebottlejunky||04-18-2001||02:20 PM||||I dunno if this is unique but..who cares..At the MI fiero fest 2000 they had the father of the fiero there..i dont know how u say his name.  But anyway I guess the first fiero in 1984 that was rolling off the line..a white SE all 4 wheels fell off and the car landed right on its belly.  I guess the machine that put on the lugs wasnt working hehe..<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||04-18-2001||02:40 PM||||86 - First year of fastback. Getrag-Muncie 5-speed is introduced with V-6, mid-year. <BR>V-6 models have voltmeter and oil pressure gauges mounted in aux pod over radio. V-6 models also get back-lighted instruments.<BR>Subwoofer (Performance Sound) system is introduced. <P>87 - Base models have redesigned front and rear fascias. Carried over to 88 base coupe and Formula. <BR>Gold paint available only in 86 and 87.  <P>EDIT - And Oreif beat me to every one of 'em.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||04-18-2001||02:40 PM||||86- first year gold was offered as color.<BR>84- coupes also had the engine vents in the center instead of on the side.<BR>87- coupes had the new fascias||||reg||1
Z||000006||johnt671||04-18-2001||03:12 PM||||I think I have that whte 84 SE that the wheels fell off.  At least that would explain a lot.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
