Z||000009||286SE'S||04-18-2001||04:09 PM||||No one mentioned the Beachwood interior color of the 88's. I have never seen one personnaly but hear they are nicer that earlier colors. I also discovered two versions of the earlier tan when getting a power-mirror door panel from an 84 to put in my 86. The 84 panel was darker almost an orange, ugly. I finally found an 87 panel that was the right color. Did I just get a panel that was NOT faded or were there two colors of tan?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||04-18-2001||04:43 PM||||Alot of people don't know this, but the 84 has a unique suspension. The later years had the same design, but the pivot points and possibly the control arms were unique to 84. They changed things in 85 to limit drop throttle oversteer and rear bumpsteer.<P>86 was the only year for a v6 4 speed SE too. Wasn't it?<P>Oops, make that a v6 4 speed SE with the GT ground effects.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 04-18-2001).]||||reg||1
