Z||000020||fiero56||04-19-2001||08:25 PM||||'87-'88 decklid stickers are different,<BR>'84 only year all 6 tail lights double as brake lights,<BR>'88 only year for factory T's,<BR>'88 only year for power lumbar,<BR>late '86 got different clutch master design,<BR>'85 only year v-6 with reflector guages,<BR>'84 only year with blakc power acc switches<BR>'84 only year with glass sails,<BR>'85-'87 v-6 had rear cooling vents for engine comp.<BR>just remembered '86 first year round trim pieces were introduced. In '87 all models had round.<BR>oh-oh, another one, '84-'86 key blanks are a different cut than '87-'88, I know, big dealm, but I love trivia and everything about these cars.<P>That's all I can think of off-hand that hasn't already been mentiond.<P>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
