Z||000022||Oreif||04-19-2001||08:48 PM||||OOps here's a few corrections.<BR>87 ~ The SE was the only car with ribbed molding. All others had smooth molding.<BR>85/86 V-6 had decal on plenum, 87/88 had etched plenum.<BR>85 and 86 SE's had V-6 with 4-spd. Some 86 SE's got the V-6/5-spd near the end of the production run.<BR>V-6 was an Option in the SE's 85 thru 87.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Songman||04-19-2001||08:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B>Not to sound negative, but...<P>Wasn't 1988 the only year Fiero with any tacky chrome trim on it?  ...The "PONTIAC" lettering on the rear fascia, you know...   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The PONTIAC lettering on my either of my 88s is not chrome. They are just sunk into the fascia. Maybe someone added the chrome or it was an option...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000024||fiero56||04-19-2001||09:05 PM||||There were only two rear fascias used in '88. Aero on fastback with no "Pontiac", and coupe style on Formula and coupe, with raised lettering(chrome was factory). There were no embossed versions in '88, had to be added after left factory.<P>The tranny things are not model dependant, just engine.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
